## Template / mirror audits (Shell only)

Use when the question is inventory-only (e.g. **which paths exist under `student/` but not under `templates/`**, or the reverse) and **Glob** cannot express it.

- **Location:** Shell tool **`working_directory`** to the repo/course root — avoid hardcoded `Set-Location` paths. Prefer a **`param` block** (`-CourseRoot`, `-SrcRoot`, `-DstRoot`, `-StartWeek`) and `Push-Location`/`try`/`finally`/`Pop-Location`.
- **Performance / correctness:** **`Resolve-Path` / canonical `$base` once** before walking files — never per-file `Resolve-Path` on the source root. Build relative paths with **`[System.IO.Path]::GetRelativePath($base, $file.FullName).Replace('\','/')`** instead of `Substring($base.Length + 1)`.
- **Validation:** `Test-Path -LiteralPath` on `$srcRoot` (and define policy for missing `$dstRoot`) before scanning; surface empty results when week dirs are expected.
- **Agent output:** Prefer a **single structured object** → **`ConvertTo-Json`** (paths used, counts, sorted `missing` / `existing` arrays) so follow-up steps do not parse `"missing: N"` prose.
- **Course weeks:** If immediate children are **`NN` two-digit weeks**, restrict with numeric **`>= StartWeek`**; align intent with [version-management SKILL](../skills/version-management/SKILL.md) sync week scope — do not guess the start week.
- **Not Python:** Do not use **`cd && python -c`** for paired-root missing-file scans — `python` is usually **not** allowlist-prefixed; quoting and path bugs are common (e.g. `replace('\\\\','/')` does not normalize `\` to `/`). Use **PS7** patterns in the skill and [cursor-command-allowlist.md §1](../docs/agent/cursor-command-allowlist.md) (*Known gaps*).
- **Still apply** the tool decision tree above (wrap compound logic in one `pwsh -NoProfile -Command`, or **`pwsh -File`** for heavy scripts).

Full worked guidance: [skills/agent-file-operations/SKILL.md](../skills/agent-file-operations/SKILL.md).

## Content identity (hash-first when path↔content continuity matters)

**Trigger:** rename / swap / path change of **binary assets** (PNG / PDF / audio / video / large data) where prior context (chat transcripts, forum links, README references, cross-session notes) asserts a specific **content-at-path** relationship. The Read tool's image-preview cache is **path-keyed**; an external rename outside Cursor (file-watcher blind spot) or in-session rename cycles can serve **stale** content for the same path.

**Recipe:**

1. **`Get-FileHash -Algorithm SHA256` first** on every candidate path; record `<sha256>  <semantic-name>` pairs in chat (or via [`scripts/Invoke-AssetHashAudit.ps1`](../scripts/Invoke-AssetHashAudit.ps1) for a folder snapshot).
2. Treat the **hash** as the identity primitive; subsequent renames are **hash-bookkeeping** only — do **not** re-Read the asset for content verification within the same task.
3. When a third party (rendered output, server response) reports content properties (image dimensions, byte size, MIME), trust those over re-reading the local preview.

**Anti-pattern (named):** *stale post-rename preview cache* — read → rename → re-read → infer content from the second preview. The second preview may not reflect the current bytes; multiple wrong-direction renames can result. Recurrence example: `logs/agent-log-global.md` 2026-05-11 08:12:29 (issue-22 screenshot loop, three rename cycles).

Worked pattern + PS7 snippet: [skills/agent-file-operations/SKILL.md § Content identity](../skills/agent-file-operations/SKILL.md). Triage class: [skills/agent-file-operations-violation-triage/SKILL.md](../skills/agent-file-operations-violation-triage/SKILL.md).

## NEVER

Absolute bans (`NEVER:` per [framework-contributing.md § Severity tags](../docs/governance/framework-contributing.md#severity-tags-mustpreferavoidnever)) — no agent exception path:

- `cmd /c` — use `pwsh`; build plus `< in > out` → [cursor-command-allowlist.md](../docs/agent/cursor-command-allowlist.md) § 1 **Build + stdin/stdout redirection (avoid `cmd`)**
- `cat` / `head` / `tail` / `sed` / `awk` / `grep` — use `Read` / `Grep` / `Glob`
- `powershell.exe` / bare `powershell -Command` — agent shell is PS7; use `pwsh`
- `Get-Date -Format` — use `-UFormat` (locale-safe); UTC: `Get-Date -AsUTC -UFormat '%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ'` — never `[System.DateTime]::UtcNow` in Shell calls
- `[ClassName]::StaticMethod(…)` / `[Class]::new()` / `New-Object` in `-Command` — includes `[System.IO.File]::`, `[System.Management.Automation.Language.Parser]::`, `[ref]` params, etc.; use PS cmdlets or `Write` a `.ps1`
- `Add-Content` on newest-first tables — prepend rows, never append
- **Any assignment as the first token** of a bare Shell call — prefix is `$var`, `$env:Path`, etc., **not** the cmdlet. Examples: `$x = Get-Content`, `$env:Path = [Environment]::GetEnvironmentVariable(...)`. Wrap the whole script in one `pwsh -NoProfile -Command "..."`, or **rewrite** to avoid the assignment (e.g. `Get-Command *cursor*` instead of splitting user PATH into `$currentPath`).
- Compound command with `;`, `&&`, `if`, `foreach`, `$LASTEXITCODE`, or `./binary` as a bare Shell call — Cursor tokenizes segments individually (see [cursor-command-allowlist.md §1](../docs/agent/cursor-command-allowlist.md) *compound command problem*). `if` and `$LASTEXITCODE` have no allowlist entry and each trigger a prompt **even when the command starts with an allowlisted prefix** (e.g. `git`). **`git` … `&& git` …** on one line is still compound — use **`working_directory`** + **one `git` subcommand per Shell call**, or one **`pwsh -NoProfile -Command`** containing all moves. For **PATH / “is this tool installed?”** checks, prefer **`Get-Command cppcheck, clang-tidy -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue`** (allowlisted prefix) instead of **`where.exe …; if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { … }`** (`where.exe` is usually off allowlist). When you truly need **`where.exe` + branching**, wrap the whole script: `pwsh -NoProfile -Command "where.exe cursor 2>`$null; if (`$LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { Write-Output 'not found' }"`.
- **Unescaped `$variable` inside a `-Command "..."` string** — the outer shell expands `$var` to empty before `pwsh` runs. In `Set-Content -Value $empty -NoNewline`, the switch name (`-NoNewline`) becomes the value argument → **file overwritten with the string `-NoNewline`, total data loss, no error**. Always escape: `` `$var ``. For read→transform→write operations, PREFER `Read` + `Write` tools instead of Shell.

## PS7 script staging

When writing a **new Shell script** for a task:

| Script intent | Where to write |
|---------------|---------------|
| Clearly **general-purpose** — `param()`, help, JSON output, Tier annotation ready | `scripts/` + catalog row in guide (decision tree §5/§6) |
| **Ad-hoc / one-off / experimental** — task-specific, not yet vetted | `scripts/_drafts/` — leave it there after use |

**Behavioural catalog scripts:** when promoting from `_drafts/` or changing policy
logic in `scripts/` / `hooks/`, use **Pester red-green TDD** per
[test-driven-development-config-scripts.md](../docs/methods/test-driven-development-config-scripts.md)
(fixture → red → green → verification chain). Say explicitly in chat that you are
in TDD mode.

**Safety tier (all workspaces):** every new or changed `.ps1` — config repo or other
project — must open `.DESCRIPTION` with `**Safety tier: N**`, a **blank help line**, then
the synopsis ([psscriptanalyzer-lint-policy.md](../docs/powershell/psscriptanalyzer-lint-policy.md) § 5).
Missing tier → external Tier 3 + Sphinx HOLD ([script-safety-gate SKILL](../skills/script-safety-gate/SKILL.md)).

**Review trigger:** before any wave-N session, when `_drafts/` has ≥5 files, or drafts are >4 weeks old — prefer a drafts-age probe if your workspace ships one; else `Glob scripts/_drafts/*.ps1`. Promote or delete stale drafts.

## Reminders

- Read tool `|` prefix = line-number metadata, not file content.
- Curated PS7 scripts (Tier 1–2, `pwsh -NoProfile -File`): [agent-file-operations-guide.md § Agent helper scripts catalog](../docs/agent/agent-file-operations-guide.md#agent-helper-scripts-catalog).
- Draft scripts (ad-hoc / not yet vetted): `scripts/_drafts/` — see § PS7 script staging above.
- PREFER targeted `Read`/`Grep`/`Glob` over 10+ file bulk reads. → [task-decomposition.mdc](task-decomposition.mdc)
- **Cross-session asset check:** when a task references a binary asset (`Screenshots/`, PDFs, audio/video) discussed in a previous session, ask: *"Has the on-disk state of `<path>` changed since the previous session?"* — if yes, run `Get-FileHash` (§ Content identity) before any rename / preview-based reasoning.
